30. WHAT PROBLEM ARE WE ACTUALLY SOLVING?
This is perhaps the most important section of the entire paper.
Naya Power is not attempting to solve every technical limitation of artificial intelligence.
That would be an impossible and misleading claim.
Instead, it targets a different problem:
THE HUMAN EXPERIENCE OF AI.
Specifically:
Problem 1 — Complexity
AI is powerful but difficult to operate effectively.
Problem 2 — Prompting
Humans often know what they want but don't know how to communicate it optimally.
Problem 3 — Context Loss
Important information disappears between sessions, tools, and models.
Problem 4 — Memory
Human beings forget.
Problem 5 — Organization
AI interactions can become fragmented and difficult to retrieve.
Problem 6 — Execution
Generating instructions is not the same as completing work.
Problem 7 — Verification
AI outputs are not automatically correct or complete.
Problem 8 — Learning
Users often receive answers without developing mastery.
Problem 9 — Personalization
Generic AI lacks deep continuity of personal context.
Problem 10 — Compounding
Most AI interactions remain isolated instead of building systematically upon one another.
Naya Power is designed around addressing these categories.

